> never named the figure herself/himself. Is brire'a a valid lujvo? I
> would prefer that over bripre, although bripre would do in a pinch.
>

brire'a is valid, but while I might consider him a person, it's a bit of a
stretch for me to consider him a human. Then again, he is your creation....

xadjai would work, since the figure is meant to embrace the bridi.
>
> I also find the word selmenli charming, and perhaps that would do.
>

Those are both interesting, but the first I feel is too metaphorical, and
neither have anything to do with his role as representing {bridi}, which I
feel is important, especially as if/when I do have him guest star, it will
be in a teaching capacity.


